xfce-md-viewer (1.0.0) noble; urgency=low

  * Initial release.
  * GTK4 + WebKitGTK viewer for Xfce (plain GTK, follows the system theme).
  * Rendering core: GFM, CommonMark, original Markdown and PHP Markdown Extra
    built in; Pandoc, MultiMarkdown and R Markdown via optional pandoc.
  * Pygments syntax highlighting. Eight built-in styles: GitHub, GitHub
    Light, GitHub Dark and GitHub Dark High Contrast (github-markdown-css
    5.9.0), Water (Water.css 2.1.1), Simple (Simple.css 2.3.7), LaTeX
    (LaTeX.css 1.14.0, with bundled Latin Modern fonts) and Plain; plus user
    styles.
  * Content security policy blocks scripts and network access in documents.
  * Viewer window: background loading/rendering, auto-reload on file change
    (keeps scroll position), local .md links open in-window with back/forward,
    external links open in the default app, find bar, zoom (saved), print /
    PDF export, drag-and-drop, Open Recent, trimmed context menu.
  * View → Flavor / Style per window; Preferences for default flavor, default
    style and opt-in remote images; custom CSS styles picked up live from
    ~/.local/share/md-viewer/styles.
  * Math (KaTeX 0.19.1) and Mermaid 12.2.0 diagrams, rendered by the viewer's
    own scripts in an isolated script world; documents still cannot run
    scripts. GitHub-style $math$, $$display$$ and ```math in GFM; pandoc math
    in pandoc flavors.
  * Table of contents sidebar (View → Show/Hide Table of Contents, F9).
  * tools/update_vendored.py and a monthly workflow keep the bundled styles,
    KaTeX and Mermaid up to date via pull requests.
  * Help menu: Keyboard Shortcuts window and Report a Problem.
  * Application icon in all standard sizes plus a scalable SVG.

 -- Tecktron Studios <software@tecktron.net>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 18:11:58 -0500
